  "question": {
    "text": "The weight of a body on the earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then weight of the body when taken to a depth half of the radius of the earth will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Zero",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The acceleration due to gravity changes with depth from the surface, which is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The given data is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Multiplying equation (i) with the mass we get the weight.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}